o  majors club and threatened them with  action richard comes back he's like ok  we came to an agreement all gonna be  fine they're gonna have their sponsors  into the go TV overlay which that's fine  like that makes perfect sense you're  putting your sponsors into the go TV  relay we're promoting them that's a  win-win for everybody that's not really  a big issue then the next day I cut a  direct message from Richard saying that  my channel had been banned and this was  like about 24 hours the past I'd say  from when they like contacted Richard  versus when I got the MCA and I didn't  know why I was banned I actually didn't  have a formal email even from twitch yet  of what had happened I'm fortunate  enough that I very good friends there  that I've just reached out to you  personally going hey what's going on and  I  this is accident which wasn't originally  I was upset with starladder but they  actually hadn't even seen the reasoning  get processed through their system yet  so they actually didn't know what  exactly i was the MC eight four they  just knew starladder had issued it and  that they had to take down my channel  now as Flom mentioned history was using  go t v-- which is an in client spectator  application that allows you to watch  games from POVs on a given server  it wasn't like anybody is watching the  stream that starladder is providing  we're not using their casters we're not  using any of their assets we're actually  watching a relay of a spectator client  that is built into the game of  counter-strike so starladder does not  own the game of counter-strike they get  the they get permission from valve to  stream the major now this is forms  first-ever ban on twitch he went public  with the info which is how most of us  heard about it and he was able to get in  touch with the guy who's in charge of  meteorites at starladder what starladder  told him is that essentially they own  the broadcast even on go TV they weren't  rude or unprofessional it was just this  is the way we've always done it this is  nothing new people have always  restreamed the major and they're telling  me now that they have exclusive rights  to it and that i actually should have  reached out to them to be able to stream  the major which that's never been done  before ever the majors have always been  to my understanding into i think the  whole community's understanding  something that we all get to watch  together we can turn on our streams as  long as we're not promoting our own  stuff we can just watch it with  everybody and there's no issue now  regarding the rights to the broadcast  starladders own rules and regulations do  state quote all broadcasting rights of  starladder major 2019 are owned by the  starladder limited this includes but is  not limited to video streams example POV  streams radio streams go TV replays  demos or TV broadcasts and quote Flom  was told nonetheless that his band would  be lifted and the next day starladder  put out a statement saying that all of  those DMCA takedown notices would be  rescinded i say all because obviously  Flom wasn't the only streamer who's  banned from twitch because of this tons  of other smaller channels were also  given the same treatment that Flom was  he even told me that starladder DMCA aid  their own official hungarian broadcast  channel which presumably was a mistake  now star letters tweet about rescinding  the DMCA takedown notices was  accompanied by a statement which read  quote the tournament license for the  csgo major grant starladder rights to  broadcast video content of the  tournament we use those rights to find  sponsorships and media contracts that  make the event possible it also notes  quote for the english language community  broadcast we will be happy to work with  community streamers if they would share  sponsorship obligations with us for more  information please contact us and quote  now given the language in that statement  and in starladders official rules and  regulations it seems entirely possible  that they could be well within their  rights to purge unauthorized broadcasts  of the major even via go TV now that  seems fine especially if they contact  the channel before trying to take them  down and explain that they need to as  starladder puts it share sponsorship  obligations with us however Flom says  that they told him that he needed to  contact them beforehand which seems  pretty unreasonable given that every  single major up until this point has  operated under a system where none of  this is necessary at this point it's all  just getting a little too murky yes so  that's why it gets really confusing is  the first time we'd ever seen that  wording is with ESL but they do not  choose to act on that that wording and  those those rights now this is the first  time that it's been acted on and the  thing is is if this is gonna change this  isn't something that you just add to a  rulebook somewhere and that someone has  to go deep into a website to go find  your rulebook and rules and stipulations  this is something that you should be  publicly stating from both sides  starladder should have mentioned hey  this is our rule set if you want to  stream it here's our terms and  conditions and here's how you stream the  major if you would like to be allowed to  and then from the other side valve if  they're selling exclusive rights to  people they need to come out and tell  everybody that they're doing that so  that way I don't get the MCA this should  be something that should be properly  conveyed and communicated at all times  there should be no disillusion - if  we're allowed to stream or not it should  be very plain text what we should and  shouldn't be allowed to stream for the  major the good news Flom channel is  indeed back and his DMCA takedown strike  is going to be apparently removed from  his twitch channel the bad news is  won't be streaming anymore of the Berlin  major until we get a more concrete  ruling on 