 recent major it seems like starladder so  far is in the driver's seat now we have  reached out to starladder for specific  comment beyond their statement on this  as of this recording they have not been  able to get back to me if and when they  do I will update you guys on their  perspective further but all this is to  say is that at this point what we really  need is a ruling from valve on go TV  just like they gave dota TV but until  that ruling is made public one way or  the other streamers like Flom are in a  gray area that they just can't cross now  to play devil's advocate here for a  second do streams like Flom Zoar the no  majors club take away valuable eyeballs  from the main starladder stream could  they potentially affect the Tio's bottom  line when it comes to hosting this major  well forum doesn't think so  if starladder wants to work side by side  with people i don't think there's any  downside to them as long as they have  their logos there we discuss it I've  actually worked with blast another  tournament organizer who has brought me  to events previously and I get to stream  there and I just provide them with my  numbers and they get to show that to  sponsors because we are providing extra  eyeballs to their sponsors and we're  adding additional value to their product  so I see no downside for them the only  downside is just by not communicating  with us and then DM saying we're taking  down or being really difficult to work  with and so here we are I ended my  interview with Flom by asking him at  this point what is the ideal resolution  for streamers like him I mean ten out of  ten would be valve coming out and  basically stating one way or the other  honestly in a perfect world I'd be  thrilled to have them and be like hey  watch it for everybody just like dota  you get to turn it on with your stream  and watch with Ustream I would also in a  perfect world they'll love to see  tournament organizers like starladder  reach out to people like me or richard  whoever to do more things together  because i'm not going away from  counter-strike I'm somebody that enjoys  counter-strike it's the game that I love  is the game that I want to stream a cm  that I want to play and I don't want to  not be able to do things with certain  tournament organizers because of bad  blood or Brent bridges I want to be able  to work with everybody do cool stuff  with them and promote the game and I  love that I've spent my entire life  playing and build it that way that  that's what I want I just want a clear  ruling and I just want an actual open  dialogue that continues moving forward  it seems kind of easy and cliche to say  but I think that's really just the best  way to go about it  thanks for watching if you want more  content like this hit the sub button and  ring that notification bell for unique  bite-sized videos you won't find  anywhere else hit up our Instagram  Twitter and Facebook pages  [Music]

